This kernel computes $out[i] = 3 \times in[i]$ via a residual connection ($2x + x$). It uses a `#pragma HLS DATAFLOW` region containing three tasks: `stageA`, `stageB`, and `stageC`. Each task executes a single loop with trip count $N=64$. Inter-task communication occurs through `hls::stream` FIFOs: `stageA` drives `s_main` and `s_skip`; `stageB` transforms `s_main` into `s_f`; `stageC` sums `s_f` and `s_skip` into `out`.

